{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the area of the convex quadrilateral with vertices \\((-1, 0)\\), \\((0, 1)\\), \\((2, 0)\\), and \\((0, -3)\\), we can use the Shoelace Theorem (also known as Gauss's area formula for polygons). The Shoelace Theorem states that for a polygon with vertices \\((x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2), \\ldots, (x_n, y_n)\\) listed in order, the area \\(A\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (x_i y_{i+1} - y_i x_{i+1}) + (x_n y_1 - y_n x_1) \\right|\n\\]\n\nFirst, we list the coordinates in order and repeat the first vertex at the end to apply the Shoelace Theorem:\n\n","prefix_end":566,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,3082,315,279,65930,29136,42939,448,17228,1124,54934,16,11,220,15,10699,701,1124,1188,15,11,220,16,10699,701,1124,1188,17,11,220,15,10699,701,323,1124,1188,15,11,481,18,10699,701,582,646,990,279,62940,301,578,576,13173,320,18654,3881,438,93216,594,3082,14806,369,68159,568,576,62940,301,578,576,13173,5302,429,369,264,29372,448,17228,1124,1188,87,62,16,11,379,62,16,701,320,87,62,17,11,379,62,17,701,1124,507,2412,11,320,87,1089,11,379,1089,10699,8,10007,304,1973,11,279,3082,17767,32,57758,374,2661,553,1447,59,9640,32,284,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,92,1124,2359,91,1124,1242,15159,72,28,16,92,47822,77,12,16,92,320,87,5318,379,15159,72,10,16,92,481,379,5318,856,15159,72,10,16,5410,488,320,87,1089,379,62,16,481,379,1089,856,62,16,8,1124,1291,7360,59,2533,5338,11,582,1140,279,13934,304,1973,323,13153,279,1156,11936,518,279,835,311,3796,279,62940,301,578,576,13173,1447,59,9640,4080,16,11,220,15,701,320,15,11,220,16,701,320,17,11,220,15,701,320,15,11,481,18,701,10293,16,11,220,15,340,59,2533,7039,11,582,3796,279,62940,301,578,576,13173,1447,59,9640,32,284,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,92,1124,2359,91,10293,16,1124,50853,220,16,488,220,15,1124,50853,220,15,488,220,17,1124,50853,48