First, we list the coordinates in order and repeat the first vertex at the end to apply the Shoelace Theorem:\n\n\\[\n(-1, 0), (0, 1), (2, 0), (0, -3), (-1, 0)\n\\]\n\nNow, we apply the Shoelace Theorem:\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| (-1 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot 0 + 2 \\cdot -3 + 0 \\cdot 0) - (0 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot 2 + 0 \\cdot 0 + -3 \\cdot -1) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression inside the absolute value:\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| (-1 + 0 - 6 + 0) - (0 + 2 + 0 + 3) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -7 - 5 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -12 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the convex quadrilateral is \\(\\boxed{6}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:198"}
